# stockroom: a manual session, in the format of the VS Code "REST Client" extension
# (send each request with "Send Request" above it). Start the service first:
#
#   cargo run -p stockroom -- migrate
#   cargo run -p stockroom -- seed --reset        # optional: 3 stores, 1000 products, stock
#   cargo run -p stockroom -- serve
#
# Watch live order events in a terminal while you go:
#
#   curl -N 'http://127.0.0.1:8080/orders/events?store=berlin-mitte'

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8080

### The process is up (does not touch the database)
GET {{base}}/healthz

### A pooled connection answers (check_connection), and the pool's state
GET {{base}}/readyz

### The database's sessions, through the simple query protocol (every value is text)
GET {{base}}/admin/sessions

### Stores
GET {{base}}/stores

### A store, with its address as the composite type `address`
POST {{base}}/stores
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "berlin-mitte",
  "name": "Berlin Mitte",
  "address": { "street": "Main 1", "city": "Berlin", "postcode": "10115", "country": "DE" }
}

### The same code again: 409, from the constraint `stores_code_key`
POST {{base}}/stores
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "berlin-mitte",
  "name": "Again",
  "address": { "street": "Main 2", "city": "Berlin", "postcode": "10115", "country": "DE" }
}

### A product; the response's ETag is its version
POST {{base}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "CHAIR-01", "name": "Garden chair", "priceCents": 4999, "tags": ["garden"], "attributes": { "color": "green" } }

### A price of zero: 422, from the constraint `products_price_positive`
POST {{base}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "CHAIR-02", "name": "Free chair", "priceCents": 0 }

### Update, if still at version 1 (send it twice: the second gets 412)
PATCH {{base}}/products/CHAIR-01
If-Match: "1"
Content-Type: application/json

{ "priceCents": 3999 }

### One page of the catalog (keyset pagination: follow nextCursor)
GET {{base}}/products?limit=5&tag=garden

### Several products in one transaction, a savepoint each: the good ones stay
POST {{base}}/products/batch
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "sku": "LAMP-01", "name": "Desk lamp", "priceCents": 2999, "tags": ["lighting"] },
  { "sku": "CHAIR-01", "name": "Duplicate", "priceCents": 1 },
  { "sku": "VASE-01", "name": "Vase", "priceCents": 1999 }
]

### A CSV price list, through COPY into a staging table and MERGE
POST {{base}}/products/import
Content-Type: text/csv

sku,name,price_cents,tags
CHAIR-01,Garden chair,4599,garden|sale
RUG-01,Rug,8999,
LAMP-01,Desk lamp,2999,lighting

### The catalog as CSV, straight from COPY … TO STDOUT
GET {{base}}/products/export.csv

### The catalog as newline-delimited JSON, row by row from a RowStream
GET {{base}}/products/stream

### Receive stock (a transaction: the level and a ledger row)
POST {{base}}/stores/berlin-mitte/stock/adjust
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "CHAIR-01", "delta": 5, "reason": "delivery" }

### Stock levels; `available` is the virtual generated column (PG 18)
GET {{base}}/stores/berlin-mitte/stock

### Place an order: reserves stock with guarded UPDATEs, pipelined
# @name placeOrder
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "store": "berlin-mitte",
  "customer": { "name": "Ada Lovelace", "email": "ada@example.com" },
  "lines": [ { "sku": "CHAIR-01", "quantity": 2 } ]
}

### More than is available: 409 insufficient_stock, and nothing reserved
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "store": "berlin-mitte",
  "customer": { "name": "Bob", "email": "bob@example.com" },
  "lines": [ { "sku": "CHAIR-01", "quantity": 99 } ]
}

### The order
GET {{base}}/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.id}}

### Pay (RETURNING old.status tells us what it was)
POST {{base}}/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.id}}/transition
If-Match: "1"
Content-Type: application/json

{ "to": "paid" }

### Skip a state: 409 invalid_transition
POST {{base}}/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.id}}/transition
Content-Type: application/json

{ "to": "collected" }

### Ready for pickup
POST {{base}}/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.id}}/transition
Content-Type: application/json

{ "to": "ready" }

### Collected: stock leaves the store, into the ledger
POST {{base}}/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.id}}/transition
Content-Type: application/json

{ "to": "collected" }

### Move stock between stores (SERIALIZABLE, retried on conflict; needs `seed` data)
POST {{base}}/stock/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "from": "store-01", "to": "berlin-mitte", "sku": "SKU00001", "quantity": 1 }

### Five aggregates, pipelined on one connection
GET {{base}}/reports/dashboard

### Sales per day
GET {{base}}/reports/sales?from=2026-01-01&to=2026-12-31

### A deliberately slow report: statement_timeout (5 s) ends it with 503 "timeout"
GET {{base}}/reports/sales?from=2026-01-01&to=2026-12-31&delayMs=7000
